      "writtenOn": "2024-12-17T18:14:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please add `Db` suffix for clarity. This also makes me wonder if the value are reasonable because even 100 dB of gain is a lot. I\u0027m not sure that hardware implementations, especially if they use fixed point samples representation internally, can cope with these ranges. I would limit the upper bound for gain to 96 dB (the theoretical dynamic range of 16-bit representation), or maybe even 90 dB to have some headroom. And use some values in between 0 and 90. I would also suggest making the negative range symmetrical to the positive range.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 647,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 647,
        "endChar": 33
      },
